WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:08.267
As the days passed, Tom started getting used to being king.

2
00:00:08.268 --> 00:00:13.594
He still wasn't comfortable in the role, and he was sometimes homesick.

3
00:00:13.595 --> 00:00:20.160
But he accepted that everyone had to bow to him and that getting dressed was a group project.

4
00:00:20.161 --> 00:00:27.781
Dining in public was supposed to begin on the fourth day of Tom's reign.

5
00:00:27.782 --> 00:00:31.872
That morning he had a meeting with his advisers.

6
00:00:31.873 --> 00:00:37.563
Lord Hertford was talking about important matters, and Tom should have been listening.

7
00:00:37.564 --> 00:00:42.023
But he was in a bad mood because he was dreading lunch.

8
00:00:42.024 --> 00:00:46.972
"Everyone will be watching me and whispering about me," he thought.

9
00:00:46.973 --> 00:00:51.233
"What if I make a mistake?"

10
00:00:51.234 --> 00:00:55.327
Tom's thoughts were interrupted by the sound of shouting outside.

11
00:00:55.328 --> 00:01:00.160
Eager for any distraction, he jumped up from the table.

12
00:01:00.161 --> 00:01:06.148
He ran to the window but couldn't see anything.

13
00:01:06.149 --> 00:01:09.597
"I wonder what's going on," Tom said.

14
00:01:09.598 --> 00:01:17.011
"I'll send a messenger to find out," Lord Hertford said.

15
00:01:17.012 --> 00:01:20.521
A few minutes later, the messenger returned.

16
00:01:20.522 --> 00:01:27.446
"A crowd is following three people—a man plus a woman and her daughter," the messenger said.

17
00:01:27.447 --> 00:01:30.811
"They've been sentenced to death."

18
00:01:30.812 --> 00:01:34.009
"To death?" Tom said.

19
00:01:34.010 --> 00:01:35.533
"Bring them here.

20
00:01:35.534 --> 00:01:43.315
I want to hear what they've done to deserve such an awful punishment."

21
00:01:43.316 --> 00:01:48.489
The three doomed prisoners soon arrived, accompanied by a sheriff.

22
00:01:48.490 --> 00:01:54.874
As they knelt before Tom, he studied their faces.

23
00:01:54.875 --> 00:01:59.973
"There's something familiar about that man," Tom thought.

24
00:01:59.974 --> 00:02:04.745
"I feel like we've met before, but that's impossible."

25
00:02:04.746 --> 00:02:08.220
He asked the sheriff what the man was accused of doing.

26
00:02:08.221 --> 00:02:11.902
The sheriff looked serious as he answered the question.

27
00:02:11.903 --> 00:02:16.001
"This criminal poisoned a man to death."

28
00:02:16.002 --> 00:02:21.604
Startled, Tom turned to the man. "Is this true?"

29
00:02:21.605 --> 00:02:28.074
"No, Your Majesty. The evidence against me is very weak."

30
00:02:28.075 --> 00:02:32.031
"I'd like to hear that evidence. Sheriff?"

31
00:02:32.032 --> 00:02:41.079
"Three witnesses say this man—a stranger—entered a house where another man lay sick in bed," the sheriff began.

32
00:02:41.080 --> 00:02:44.040
"It was ten o'clock in the morning.

33
00:02:44.041 --> 00:02:48.439
The sick man was alone at the time and sleeping.

34
00:02:48.440 --> 00:02:54.973
This man soon left the house, and the sick man died within the hour."

35
00:02:54.974 --> 00:03:00.839
"Did anyone see this man give poison to the sick man?" Tom asked.

36
00:03:00.840 --> 00:03:04.112
"Was any poison ever found?"

37
00:03:04.113 --> 00:03:07.118
"No, Your Majesty."

38
00:03:07.119 --> 00:03:10.206
Tom scratched his head and looked puzzled.

39
00:03:10.207 --> 00:03:15.414
"Then how do you know he was poisoned?"

40
00:03:15.415 --> 00:03:20.233
"The doctors said his symptoms could only be caused by poisoning.

41
00:03:20.234 --> 00:03:26.950
And there's more: A while ago a witch told several people that the man would be poisoned.

42
00:03:26.951 --> 00:03:33.193
And . . . " The sheriff took a deep breath for dramatic effect.

43
00:03:33.194 --> 00:03:38.271
"That a stranger would give the poison!"

44
00:03:38.272 --> 00:03:45.850
Tom was not impressed. "Most of the world is made up of strangers."

45
00:03:45.851 --> 00:03:52.204
"That's true," one of Tom's advisers whispered to Lord Hertford, who nodded in agreement.

46
00:03:52.205 --> 00:03:55.846
"Yes, Your Majesty," the sheriff said.

47
00:03:55.847 --> 00:04:04.071
"But the witch said that the stranger would have brown hair and wear plain clothing just like this man."

48
00:04:04.072 --> 00:04:07.678
It was hard for Tom to argue with that.

49
00:04:07.679 --> 00:04:11.992
"What do you have to say for yourself?" Tom asked the man.

50
00:04:11.993 --> 00:04:16.669
"Can any of your friends speak on your behalf?"

51
00:04:16.670 --> 00:04:20.971
"No, Your Majesty." The man looked sad.

52
00:04:20.972 --> 00:04:27.127
"As you've already heard, I'm a stranger here, so I have no friends.

53
00:04:27.128 --> 00:04:32.066
But if I may speak in my own defense . . ."

54
00:04:32.067 --> 00:04:36.472
Tom nodded to grant him permission.

55
00:04:36.473 --> 00:04:40.144
"I'm accused of poisoning a man.

56
00:04:40.145 --> 00:04:45.029
But at that exact moment, I wasn't taking a life.

57
00:04:45.030 --> 00:04:49.294
In fact I was saving a life!

58
00:04:49.295 --> 00:04:52.283
A boy was drowning—"

59
00:04:52.284 --> 00:04:58.287
Tom held up his hand for silence because he suddenly recognized this man.

60
00:04:58.288 --> 00:05:02.763
"He's the one who pulled Julian from the river!" Tom thought.

61
00:05:02.764 --> 00:05:05.834
"But I have to be sure."

62
00:05:05.835 --> 00:05:11.868
"On what date is he accused of committing this crime?" Tom asked the sheriff.

63
00:05:11.869 --> 00:05:15.337
"Well, that's easy for me to remember."

64
00:05:15.338 --> 00:05:22.429
The sheriff puffed up his chest with pride. "It was New Year's Day!"

65
00:05:22.430 --> 00:05:27.858
"The same day that Julian almost drowned!" Tom thought.

66
00:05:27.859 --> 00:05:30.763
"Let the prisoner go free!

67
00:05:30.764 --> 00:05:34.800
It is the king's will!" Tom shouted.

68
00:05:34.801 --> 00:05:42.406
"That other man may have been poisoned, but it wasn't by this man."

69
00:05:42.407 --> 00:05:46.328
Tom was momentarily embarrassed by his outburst.

70
00:05:46.329 --> 00:05:48.486
But he quickly recovered.

71
00:05:48.487 --> 00:05:55.835
"I'm enraged that a man was sentenced to death based on such ridiculous evidence," Tom went on.

72
00:05:55.836 --> 00:06:00.962
"Such gossip shouldn't even be called evidence."

73
00:06:00.963 --> 00:06:07.174
A low buzz of admiration for Tom's intelligence went around the table.

74
00:06:07.175 --> 00:06:12.563
"The king asked such good questions," one adviser said to another.

75
00:06:12.564 --> 00:06:18.542
"I don't see any signs of illness in the boy," the second adviser said.

76
00:06:18.543 --> 00:06:22.964
Lord Hertford rapped on the table to get the advisers' attention.

77
00:06:22.965 --> 00:06:27.458
"Now let's resume our discussion of the royal stables. The horses—"

78
00:06:27.459 --> 00:06:30.932
"Just a minute," Tom interrupted.

79
00:06:30.933 --> 00:06:41.915
"I want to hear what the other two prisoners have to say!"

